{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "hjweno_norm_1d_eikonal_mms",
    "description": "Method-of-manufactured-solutions order-of-accuracy driver for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/hjweno_norm_D1_periodic on the periodic unit interval [0,1]. Forced-steady eikonal / Hamilton-Jacobi equation u_t = -S|u_x| + S|g'(x)| with the manufactured solution g(x) = sin(2 pi x): because u_t = -S|g'| + S|g'| = 0, g is the EXACT solution of the continuous forced PDE for all t, so the analytic reference at every time is g itself. The forcing S|g'(x)| = 2 pi S |cos(2 pi x)| is the constant-in-time source that balances the operator. Discretely u_t = S*(|g'| - hjweno(u)); starting from u(0) = g the imbalance is the fifth-order Hamilton-Jacobi WENO truncation error S*(|g'| - hjweno(g)) = O(dx^5), so the discrete solution drifts from g at rate O(dx^5) and the L2 / Linf error at the assert time falls as O(dx^5) (expected order 5). THE CRITICAL POINTS ARE NOT A PROBLEM: g is SMOOTH everywhere (it is |u_x| that has kinks, at x = 1/4, 3/4 where cos changes sign, not u), so the WENO-Z one-sided derivative reconstructions u_x^± approximate u_x = 2 pi cos(2 pi x) to O(dx^5) everywhere INCLUDING the first-order critical points u_x = 0 at x = 1/4, 3/4 (u_xx != 0 there) where classic Jiang-Shu weights would drop to ~fourth order; the WENO-Z weights tau_5 = |beta_0 - beta_2| restore the full fifth order (Borges 2008, Henrick 2005), and the Godunov max/min entropy fix selects the correct one-sided branch through the |grad| kinks. Numerically verified: pairwise orders 5.00 -> 5.00 across N = 16..256 in BOTH L2 and Linf (de-risked in numpy: |g'| - hjweno(g) falls at exactly fifth order; the integrated forced-steady error matches). Both g and |g'| are periodic (g(0)=g(1)=0, |cos| has period 1/2), so the periodic wrap is fully consistent (no seam artifact); the six wrap faces converge at the same fifth-order rate as the interior, so the state L2/Linf reduction over the whole field is a clean order-5 gate with nothing to exempt. The grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0,1]: x0 = 0 and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing the extent by the metaparameter name N, esm-spec 9.7.6, so the loader-API rebinding of N for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent). The ic, the forcing observed, and the test reference spell the cell-center coordinate x_i = (i - 1/2)/N inline from literals and the metaparameter N (the 6.6.5/ic build-time cellwise evaluation is scope-free). Per-resolution error norms are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/hjweno_norm_1d_eikonal_mms/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:hamilton_jacobi",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Peng, D. (2000). Weighted ENO Schemes for Hamilton-Jacobi Equations. SIAM Journal on Scientific Computing, 21(6), 2126-2143. Fifth-order HJ-WENO reconstruction of the one-sided derivatives combined by the Godunov Hamiltonian.",
        "doi": "10.1137/S106482759732455X"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Borges, R., Carmona, M., Costa, B., & Don, W. S. (2008). An improved weighted essentially non-oscillatory scheme for hyperbolic conservation laws. Journal of Computational Physics, 227(6), 3191-3211. The WENO-Z weights that recover fifth order at the critical points u_x = 0 of the smooth manufactured profile.",
        "doi": "10.1016/j.jcp.2007.11.038"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Rouy, E., & Tourin, A. (1992). A viscosity solutions approach to shape-from-shading. SIAM Journal on Numerical Analysis, 29(3), 867-884. Convergence of the Godunov Hamiltonian to the viscosity solution of the eikonal equation.",
        "doi": "10.1137/0729053"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "HJWenoEikonalMMS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/hjweno_norm_D1_periodic.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Level-set field integrated under the forced eikonal u_t = -S*hjweno(u) + S|g'|; starts at and stays near the manufactured solution g(x) = sin(2 pi x), deviating by the O(dx^5) HJ-WENO truncation error."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Non-negative Hamilton-Jacobi speed (u_t = -S|u_x|). The forcing carries the matching S so g is the exact steady solution for any S > 0."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "expression": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "N"
            ]
          },
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "forcing": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "The manufactured source |g'(x)| = 2 pi |cos(2 pi x_i)| (the S factor is folded via the du/dt scaling; x_i = (i - 1/2)/N spelled inline). It exactly balances the continuous operator so g = sin(2 pi x) is the steady exact solution; the residual after discretization is the O(dx^5) truncation error.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                6.283185307179586,
                {
                  "op": "abs",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "cos",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            6.283185307179586,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "sin",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  6.283185307179586,
                  {
                    "op": "aggregate",
                    "output_idx": [
                      "i"
                    ],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": {
                      "i": {
                        "from": "x"
                      }
                    },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "i",
                            0.5
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "/",
                          "args": [
                            1,
                            "N"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "S",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "forcing",
                  {
                    "op": "sqrt",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "^",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "D",
                            "args": [
                              "u"
                            ],
                            "wrt": "x"
                          },
                          2
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_eikonal",
          "description": "Manufactured solution g(x) = sin(2 pi x), S = 1. u_t = -S|u_x| + S|g'| with u(0) = g gives u_t = 0 at the continuous level, so g is exact for all t; discretely u_t = S*(|g'| - hjweno(u)) and the initial imbalance is the fifth-order truncation S*(|g'| - hjweno(g)) = O(dx^5), so ||u(T) - g|| = O(dx^5). References evaluate g at x_i = (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5. The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (L2_error 0 within 1e-9). The t=0.1 assertion bounds the fifth-order error (about 6.7e-8 L2 at N=64, far under the 1e-3 cap). Exact per-resolution L2/Linf errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/hjweno_norm_1d_eikonal_mms/golden/errors.json; the observed order is asserted 5.0 +/- 0.3 by scripts/check_convergence_order.py.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.1
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.001
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
